nlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" read a function as a getter, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" reacts through a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"computed"},{"type":"text","value":": a function there is the query function itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you instead pass a getter for the whole options object ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery(() => ({ ... }))"},{"type":"text","value":"), every option\ninside it — including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"retry"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" — is re-evaluated whenever the getter's own\nreactive dependencies change, since the entire object is recomputed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" only re-runs when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" changes, or when the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" function's own reference changes. Since a\nVue "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setup()"},{"type":"text","value":" function runs only once per component instance, an inline "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" function passed directly\nto "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" already has a stable reference across reactive updates. An inline "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":"\ncreated inside a whole-options getter is recreated — and so can change reference — every time that getter\nre-evaluates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tqueryfndata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"terror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"link","href":"DefaultError.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DefaultError"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of errors your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" may throw."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" ends up as after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" runs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tquerydata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryData"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of data stored in the cache, before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" runs. Defaults to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryFnData"},{"type":"text","value":" and can be configured independently of it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tquerykey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TQueryKey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TQueryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"QueryKey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryKey"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"link","href":"QueryKey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryKey"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tqueryfndata","text":"TQueryFnData","level":3},{"id":"terror","text":"TError","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"tquerydata","text":"TQueryData","level":3},{"id":"tquerykey","text":"TQueryKey","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype UseQueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey> = MaybeRef<{ [Property in keyof QueryObserverOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>]: Property extends \"enabled\" | \"queryKey\" ? QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property] : Property extends \"queryFn\" ? MaybeRefDeep<QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property] | SkipTokenForUseQuery> : MaybeRefDeep<QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property]> } & ShallowOption>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-query/src/queryOptions.ts:90](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/vue-query/src/queryOptions.ts#L90)\n\nThe options accepted by `queryOptions`, `useQuery`, and the other query hooks. `enabled` tracks reactive\ndependencies automatically as a `ref`, a plain value, or a reactive getter (`() => ...`). `queryKey` reacts\nthrough a `ref` or a reactive getter for the array itself, or `ref`s and reactive getters as individual\nentries. Other options are read once when passed as a plain value, and stay reactive when passed as a `ref`\nor a `computed`. Only `enabled` and `queryKey` read a function as a getter, so `queryFn` reacts through a\n`computed`: a function there is the query function itself.\n\nIf you instead pass a getter for the whole options object (`useQuery(() => ({ ... }))`), every option\ninside it — including `staleTime`, `retry`, and `select` — is re-evaluated whenever the getter's own\nreactive dependencies change, since the entire object is recomputed.\n\n`select` only re-runs when `data` changes, or when the `select` function's own reference changes. Since a\nVue `setup()` function runs only once per component instance, an inline `select` function passed directly\nto `queryOptions`/`useQuery` already has a stable reference across reactive updates. An inline `select`\ncreated inside a whole-options getter is recreated — and so can change reference — every time that getter\nre-evaluates.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\nThe type your `queryFn` resolves to.\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](DefaultError.md)\n\nThe type of errors your `queryFn` may throw.\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\nThe type `data` ends up as after `select` runs.\n\n### TQueryData\n\n`TQueryData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\nThe type of data stored in the cache, before `select` runs. Defaults to\n`TQueryFnData` and can be configured independently of it.\n\n### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* [`QueryKey`](QueryKey.md) = [`QueryKey`](QueryKey.md)\n\nThe type of your `queryKey`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: UseQueryOptions\ntitle: UseQueryOptions\n---\n\n```ts\ntype UseQueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey> = MaybeRef<{ [Property in keyof QueryObserverOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>]: Property extends \"enabled\" | \"queryKey\" ? QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property] : Property extends \"queryFn\" ? MaybeRefDeep<QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property] | SkipTokenForUseQuery> : MaybeRefDeep<QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryData, TQueryKey>[Property]> } & ShallowOption>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/vue-query/src/queryOptions.ts:90](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/vue-query/src/queryOptions.ts#L90)\n\nThe options accepted by `queryOptions`, `useQuery`, and the other query hooks. `enabled` tracks reactive\ndependencies automatically as a `ref`, a plain value, or a reactive getter (`() => ...`). `queryKey` reacts\nthrough a `ref` or a reactive getter for the array itself, or `ref`s and reactive getters as individual\nentries. Other options are read once when passed as a plain value, and stay reactive when passed as a `ref`\nor a `computed`. Only `enabled` and `queryKey` read a function as a getter, so `queryFn` reacts through a\n`computed`: a function there is the query function itself.\n\nIf you instead pass a getter for the whole options object (`useQuery(() => ({ ... }))`), every option\ninside it — including `staleTime`, `retry`, and `select` — is re-evaluated whenever the getter's own\nreactive dependencies change, since the entire object is recomputed.\n\n`select` only re-runs when `data` changes, or when the `select` function's own reference changes. Since a\nVue `setup()` function runs only once per component instance, an inline `select` function passed directly\nto `queryOptions`/`useQuery` already has a stable reference across reactive updates. An inline `select`\ncreated inside a whole-options getter is recreated — and so can change reference — every time that getter\nre-evaluates.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\nThe type your `queryFn` resolves to.\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](DefaultError.md)\n\nThe type of errors your `queryFn` may throw.\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\nThe type `data` ends up as after `select` runs.\n\n### TQueryData\n\n`TQueryData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\nThe type of data stored in the cache, before `select` runs. Defaults to\n`TQueryFnData` and can be configured independently of it.\n\n### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* [`QueryKey`](QueryKey.md) = [`QueryKey`](QueryKey.md)\n\nThe type of your `queryKey`.\n"}
